val loop entered from"] [183 2 "// C), which CPython 3.14 measures on the machine's stack and pyi counts (enterRecursiveCall)"] [185 2 "// direct is the number of direct calls (callDirect: a compiled caller's Go frames under its compiled callee's"] [186 2 "// loop) nested on the thread's Go stack, at most directMax (queue 216d)"] [188 26 "// the containers being repr'd (Py_ReprEnter)"] [189 26 "// callStack's signal, reused (202b)"] [190 2 "// asyncio_running_loop and asyncio_running_task of the thread state (_asyncio, queue 224), nil when none"] [192 30 "// the current context (context.c: the thread state's), nil until first asked"] [193 2 "// finPend are the objects with a __del__ this thread's frames made, not yet checked at a frame's return, and"] [194 2 "// finPendDepth the deepest of their frames' depths, 0 when none (finalize.go's finAtReturn: the moment at a frame's"] [195 2 "// return, the user's decision of 2026-11-22)"] [200 1 "// CurrentHandled is the exception being handled (_PyErr_GetTopmostException): this level's slot, else the"] [201 1 "// first not None of the levels it was resumed from; None when none is."] [214 1 "// chainContext is _PyErr_SetObject's implicit chaining: exc's __context__ the exception being handled, a cycle"] [215 1 "// through exc in that chain cut first."] [233 10 "// a cycle not through exc"] [243 1 "// reprEnter is Py_ReprEnter: true when o is already being repr'd (a recursive container: \"[...]\")."] [255 1 "// reprLeave is Py_ReprLeave."] [258 1 "// The C level's stack (PY7). CPython 3.14 raises RecursionError \"Stack overflow (used N kB)WHERE\" when a guarded"] [259 1 "// built-in call (_Py_EnterRecursiveCall) finds the machine's stack past its soft limit; a Python frame does not use it."] [260 1 "// pyi's built-ins recurse on Go's stack, a goroutine's at most 1 GB, which a deep enough structure overflowed (a fatal"] [261 1 "// Go error: test_tuple's test_hash_deeply_nested, test_copy's reflexive comparisons, test_isinstance's recursions)."] [262 1 "// pyi counts the guarded levels instead, and Go's calls into the machine (Thread.run: the eval loop entered from C,"] [263 1 "// where \"\"): cStackLevels of them, cFrameBytes each as the message's nominal kB (about"] [264 1 "// CPython's 1 MB soft limit on Linux); CPython's own depth varies with the call (on Alpine aarch64 a tuple's hash"] [265 1 "// reaches 10,000 levels, its repr not)."] [271 1 "// enterRecursiveCall is _Py_EnterRecursiveCall(where): false, with the RecursionError, past the limit; else the"] [272 1 "// level is entered and leaveRecursiveCall leaves it."] [285 1 "// stackOverflow is _Py_CheckRecursiveCall's RecursionError."] [290 1 "// leaveRecursiveCall is _Py_LeaveRecursiveCall for enterRecursiveCall's thread."] [299 1 "// currentThread is the running thread (the GIL's holder)."] [302 1 "// unbound is the marker :load-fast-and-clear pushes for an unbound local (PEP 709)."] [309 1 "// newFrame makes the frame of a function's call with its arguments bound (CPython's"] [310 1 "// _PyEval_MakeFrameVector); args holds the positional then the keyword arguments."] [321 3 "// the fast locals and the value stack in one allocation (202b): the stack's room the most the code's"] [322 3 "// frames have needed (Code.stackHint, kept by runFrames at a return), so a call does not grow it from nothing"] [328 3 "// a module's or a class body's code called as a function (types.FunctionType(code, globals): the asyncio REPL's"] [329 3 "// statements, queue 293): its names are the globals, as _PyFunction_Vectorcall gives _PyEval_Vector the"] [330 3 "// function's globals as the frame's locals for a code without CO_OPTIMIZED"] [341 13 "// _tracemalloc's allocation (queue 220): the caller's, the callee not entered yet"] [356 1 "// bindArgs puts a call's arguments into the parameters' slots (positional, *args, keyword-only,"] [357 1 "// **kwargs, then the defaults), raising CPython's TypeErrors (Python/ceval.c's, with the qualified name)."] [